# Supabase — test data needs no ask

Founder standing rule (2026-08-07): **Do not prompt for approval** for Supabase SQL / Admin API / MCP `execute_sql` / row deletes when the change is **only test / e2e fixture data**.

## In scope (proceed without asking)

- Users/emails/phones clearly marked `e2e*` / `e2e.*` / Account B style fixtures from platform-truth W0
- Events named `e2e-*` and their child rows (guests, collabs, media, etc.)
- Cleaning/resetting those fixtures between tests
- Seeding disposable data under the same naming convention

## Out of scope (still ask / use Smart Mode approval)

- Schema DDL, RLS policies, GRANT/REVOKE, function replacements affecting **all** tenants
- Mutations to real non-`e2e` events or production host accounts
- Anything that changes security posture for the live shared project beyond test rows

If unsure whether a change is test-only, ask once.
